{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217283-2e-municipal-charms-question","id":1217283,"title":"2E - Municipal Charms question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-09T23:47:21-07:00","id":1217283,"title":"2E - Municipal Charms question","content":"I am thinking about the Municipal Charms that Alchemicals wield, and I would like to other people\u2019s opinions on what sort of Essence Level Municipal Charm it should take to cap a level 5 Demesne and redirect all of its Essence back to the metropoli. I will go out on a limb and just conclude for an N/A Demesne it will automatically require Essence 10 and possibly constant maintenance of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T02:20:42-07:00","id":1217304,"title":"","content":"I'd not limit the cost of those charms by the essence, but by the fact that they do need to actually be crafted and installed. In the case of normal charms this cost is relatively low and can be mostly ignored by mechanics, but a Municipal Charm allowing the Alchemical city to cap a level 5 demesne would be, in cost and effort required, probably not so much different than building a level 5 Manse.<br /> Essence 8 (so, the lowest level at which we can even start talking about Municipal Charms) should be perfectly fine.<br /> And N/A demesne would almost certainly require much, much more effort than simply buying a charm. It would be a massive architectural and engineering undertaking in its own. Probably on a level of a miracle working even for E10 Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> Personally though i'd simply make it a Municipal Charm that would allow the Alchemical to draw power from an already existing nearby manse","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 05-10-2018, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T09:51:45-07:00","id":1217430,"title":"","content":"Something to note: a Vat complex is an E8 charm, the first all cities get, and there are rules for making one out of a 5 dot manse. So 5 dot manse and E8 alchemical charm are VERY ROUGHLY equal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T13:45:06-07:00","id":1217486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217283-2e-municipal-charms-question?p=1217430#post1217430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to note: a Vat complex is an E8 charm, the first all cities get, and there are rules for making one out of a 5 dot manse. So 5 dot manse and E8 alchemical charm are VERY ROUGHLY equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is sort of what I was getting at. In the Autocthonia book it mentioned how wind turbines were helping to power one of the cities and thus reduces the resources that cities consume to power its Charms. I am actually referring to a Charm that can be detached from the city, or at least exist outside of the city but is attached miles long cables, and can transform a Demesne into an energy source for the city, thus giving the overworked populace a reduced work load and aids with the crippling shortages that are being experienced all over the Autocthonia. This of course presupposes that the city exists outside of Autocthonia and on Creation probably built on a Level 5 Demesne. Or perhaps that there is some way for the Charm to exist and transmit across Realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 05-10-2018, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T20:21:39-07:00","id":1217567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217283-2e-municipal-charms-question?p=1217486#post1217486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... perhaps that there is some way for the Charm to exist and transmit across Realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>There almost certainly is, and I suggest it incorporate prayer heavily. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T20:50:53-07:00","id":1217575,"title":"","content":"I believe the Alchemicals or Autocthonia book actually gives some idea of how powerful a municipal charm would need to be in order to open a gateway to Creation.<br /> Edit: Opening a gate to Creation is only an essence 8 muncipal charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T11:53:26-07:00","id":1217735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217283-2e-municipal-charms-question?p=1217575#post1217575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the Alchemicals or Autocthonia book actually gives some idea of how powerful a municipal charm would need to be in order to open a gateway to Creation.<br /> Edit: Opening a gate to Creation is only an essence 8 muncipal charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also says it is easy to do from that side, but even the FA Solars couldn't do it from the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T14:28:52-07:00","id":1217776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217283-2e-municipal-charms-question?p=1217735#post1217735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also says it is easy to do from that side, but even the FA Solars couldn't do it from the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but that's still surprisingly easy even in light of the Seal of Eight Divinities not being meant to keep them in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T18:07:10-07:00","id":1218113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217283-2e-municipal-charms-question?p=1217776#post1217776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, but that's still surprisingly easy even in light of the Seal of Eight Divinities not being meant to keep them in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the nature of the Seal. For all we know all you need to do to open it from their side is send a politely worded request to the Design and the charm is needed to send the billion copies to each Design Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T21:04:47-07:00","id":1218143,"title":"","content":"Maybe it was because the FA Solars tried to do everything by overpowering it with their awesomness. Maybe the Seal was designed to open to a lighter touch but resist a powerful one (and thus keep the Solars out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T21:35:29-07:00","id":1218146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217283-2e-municipal-charms-question?p=1218143#post1218143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it was because the FA Solars tried to do everything by overpowering it with their awesomness. Maybe the Seal was designed to open to a lighter touch but resist a powerful one (and thus keep the Solars out</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't quite make sense, considering the most success the first age solars had was putting a protoshinmaic vortex of all things into a Hand of the Great Maker, which managed to briefly open 7/8 of the seal. As in, so briefly that they couldn't possibly attempt anything to open seal #8.<br /> it's just that the seal was legitimately built to be one way only. What keeps people IN autocthonia is that it's in Elsewhere, with no normal physical connection to Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}